Cargo.lock

# Porter scratch: the per-slot brief and its raw stdout. These were once
# committed by a porter running `git add -A`. Because their content differs
# per worktree by construction, every subsequent merge conflicted on them and
# the transpile loop wedged for eight days. The loop now writes briefs outside
# the worktree entirely; this is the second line of defence.
.port-task.md
.port.out
